title: Libraries
card: Chapter 10 | Libraries | More words, for more things
say:
  The language itself is small. Libraries give it more words: for maths, time, files and folders, databases, the web, sound, windows and games.
  A library loads by itself as soon as a program uses one of its words. Writing use, and its name, at the top says so out loud.
uncard

new: libraries.stella
type fast:
  use: maths
  use: time
  use: patterns

  genesis:
    scrawl "Sine of 30 is ", sine of 30
    scrawl "2 to the power 10 is ", power of (2, 10)
    scrawl "17 shared by 5 leaves ", remainder of (17, 5)
    scrawl "Christmas 2026 is a ", weekday of "2026-12-25"
    scrawl "A month after 13 November: ", date plus days ("2026-11-13", 30)
    set line to "Sam scored 31, Jo scored 7"
    scrawl matches of the pattern with ("[0-9]+", line)
    scrawl replace the pattern with ("[0-9]+", line, "#")
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 5-10
spot: lines 6-8
say:
  From maths: sine, cosine and tangent, in degrees. Power of, remainder of, rounding, pi, and logarithms.
spot: line 9
say: From time: wait, the time now, today, and dates. Dates are text like twenty twenty six, twelve, twenty five, so they sort and save as they are.
spot: line 10
say: Date plus days counts forward, or back with a number below zero.
spot: off
zoom: lines 11-13
spot: line 12
say:
  The patterns library finds text by its shape. Zero to nine in square brackets, then plus, means one or more digits.
  So matches of the pattern finds every number in the line.
spot: line 13
say: And replace the pattern changes each one.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out

say: A few more: folders, databases, and letters.
clear
type fast:
  use: folders
  use: database
  use: letters

  genesis:
    make the folder "notes"
    inscribe "hello" into file "notes/a.txt"
    scrawl files in the folder "notes"
    change the database ("shop.db", "create table if not exists items (name text, price real)")
    change the database with values ("shop.db", "insert into items values (?, ?)", a list containing ("tea", "2.5"))
    scrawl rows from the database ("shop.db", "select name, price from items")
    scrawl code of the letter "A", " ", the letter with code 233
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 6-8
say:
  Folders makes, lists, moves, copies and erases files and folders.
zoom: lines 9-11
say:
  Database keeps data in an SQLite file, with SQL, the language databases speak. A question mark stands for each value, so text that people type can't change the command.
zoom: line 12
say: And letters turns a letter into the number behind it, and back again.
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out

say:
  There are more. The web library fetches and sends web pages. Server makes your program a web server. Sound plays sounds and music.
  Computer runs other programs, and spreadsheet reads and writes CSV files. Every one of their words is in the list on the left.
click: #word-search
type: weekday
zoom: #side
say: Searching shows what a word means, and how to use it.
wait
zoom: out
focus

card: Chapter 10 | Making a library | How a word is made
say: So how is a library made? Here is the time library's own file.
uncard
open library: time
line: 30
zoom: lines 28-30
spot: line 28
say:
  Each word says what it means in C++, for programs that are built, after the equals sign.
  Seconds in curly brackets stands for the input.
spot: line 29
say: The runs line says what it means in Python, for running directly.
spot: line 30
say: And the web line says what it means in JavaScript, for programs made into web pages.
spot: off
zoom: out
say:
  So anything C++, Python or JavaScript can do, can be given an English word this way. A library file can sit in the libraries folder, or right next to your program.
